/* Status. Every value comes from a token; nothing here is a literal colour.

   Specimen 3b draws the four cards in one row under "STATUS MESSAGE · centre
   of scene": a 64px card at radius.lg with a 3px edge, the word in the display
   face, in capitals, and a fill per state. design/twins/3b.json measures ours
   against the drawing. */

.gs-status {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: var(--gs-space-gap);

  /* The drawing's 64px is a floor rather than a height. A translated word is
     longer than the English one, and a card with a fixed height puts the
     second line outside itself (docs/boundaries.md: a label wraps, and the
     layout gives way). GO! is one syllable in English and three in Polish. */
  min-block-size: var(--gs-size-action-large);
  padding: var(--gs-space-2) var(--gs-space-3);

  border: var(--gs-stroke-ui) solid var(--gs-color-edge);
  border-radius: var(--gs-radius-lg);
  background: var(--gs-color-surface);
  color: var(--gs-color-ink);
}

/* The word. The display face comes from .gs-display-type, so a theme that
   changes the face reaches this card without the card naming it. The size and
   the weight are read per state from the role each state draws at, because
   the display token's own weight is 800 in arcade and the specimen draws all
   four words at 900: taking the weight from the face made this the one piece
   of display type in the library a stop lighter than the drawing, which the
   3b twin caught.

   READY is the drawing's 22px at 900, which is type.stat exactly. */
.gs-status__value {
  min-inline-size: 0;
  font-size: var(--gs-type-stat-font-size);
  font-weight: var(--gs-type-stat-font-weight);
  letter-spacing: var(--gs-type-label-letter-spacing);
  line-height: var(--gs-type-title-line-height);
  text-align: center;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  /* A word that cannot fit the card breaks inside itself rather than beside
     it. Never truncated: a status the player can only half read is worse than
     a status on two lines. */
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}

/* GO!, the moment the round starts. The drawing fills it positive, inks it
   on-bright, steps the word up to 28px and rings it in a 28px green glow.

   The size is type.score. The drawing's 28 has no token, and the first answer
   here was type.title, on the reasoning that 24 sits between READY's 22 and
   type.score's 36. That reasoning only held in the default theme. Arcade is
   the theme the drawing is, and arcade sets title to 20px and stat to 22, so
   GO! came out smaller than the READY it is supposed to shout over: the one
   relationship the specimen is drawing was inverted in the only theme that
   matters to it. Score is the sole token above stat in both themes, 34 in
   arcade and 36 in the default against the drawn 28, so GO! is now louder
   than drawn rather than quieter. A 28px display step is the token request,
   and design/scale.json counts five uses of it, so it clears the evidence
   test; this reads score until it lands.

   The glow is the positive colour at the space.8 radius, the nearest token to
   the drawing's 28px. `-solid` rather than the plain token because a theme may
   set colour.positive to a gradient, and a gradient in a box-shadow is an
   invalid declaration the browser drops without saying so.

   The drawing's resting `transform: scale(1.04)` is deliberately not here. The
   same note on the specimen says READY→GO plays motion.pop, and gs-pop lands
   on scale(1): a resting 1.04 under a keyframe that ends at 1 makes the card
   jump the moment the pop finishes. The fill, the ink, the size and the glow
   are four changes already, and the pop is the swell the drawing is after. */
.gs-status[data-gs-value='go'] {
  background: var(--gs-color-positive);
  border-color: var(--gs-color-edge);
  color: var(--gs-color-on-bright);
  box-shadow: 0 0 var(--gs-space-8) var(--gs-color-positive-solid);
}

.gs-status[data-gs-value='go'] .gs-status__value {
  font-size: var(--gs-type-score-font-size);
  font-weight: var(--gs-type-score-font-weight);
}

/* PAUSED. Held, not finished: the quietest of the four, drawn on the edge fill
   with the brighter edge around it and the secondary ink. */
.gs-status[data-gs-value='paused'] {
  background: var(--gs-color-edge);
  border-color: var(--gs-color-edge-high);
  color: var(--gs-color-ink-secondary);
}

/* COMPLETE. The round has settled, so it wears the reward fill. */
.gs-status[data-gs-value='complete'] {
  background: var(--gs-color-reward);
  border-color: var(--gs-color-edge);
  color: var(--gs-color-on-bright);
}

/* Both are the drawing's 18px at 900. type.action is 19 in arcade and is the
   closest number, and reading it here is wrong twice over: a status card is
   not something a player presses, and tests/lib/check-theme-axes.mjs refuses
   a stylesheet that declares the action axis by hand, because the next
   property added to that axis would not reach a component that copied two of
   them. type.title is the heading role, 20px at 900 in arcade, two out rather
   than one, and it is the right kind of token for a word that heads a card.
   The face stays the display one from .gs-display-type; the size and weight
   are borrowed, the way reward's compact cell borrows the label size for a
   display-face word. */
.gs-status[data-gs-value='paused'] .gs-status__value,
.gs-status[data-gs-value='complete'] .gs-status__value {
  font-size: var(--gs-type-title-font-size);
  font-weight: var(--gs-type-title-font-weight);
}

/* The display shadow belongs to READY alone.
 *
 * The specimen draws `text-shadow: 0 3px 0 var(--edge)` on the READY card and
 * on none of the other three, and it is right to: READY sits on the surface
 * fill and needs the lift, while GO!, PAUSED and COMPLETE sit on their own
 * fills where a dark shadow under bright ink reads as a smudge. Taking the
 * shadow from .gs-display-type gave it to all four. A theme that turns the
 * display shadow off still turns READY's off, because READY reads the token
 * and this only removes it from the three the drawing leaves clean. */
.gs-status:not([data-gs-value='ready']) .gs-status__value {
  text-shadow: none;
}

/* The pause mark: two bars before the word, in the card's own ink. Drawn as
   two elements rather than one drawing, because two rectangles are not a
   glyph. The full radius on a 4px bar is a 2px corner, which is what the
   drawing draws. */
.gs-status__bars {
  display: flex;
  flex: none;
  gap: var(--gs-space-1);
}

.gs-status__bar {
  inline-size: var(--gs-space-1);
  block-size: var(--gs-space-4);
  border-radius: var(--gs-radius-full);
  background: currentColor;
}
